%% Persistence: a download's lifecycle across an app restart.
%% Statuses are JobStatus in history.rs; the file is <app data dir>/downloads.json.
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Queued: start_download (no startAt / past startAt)
    [*] --> Scheduled: start_download (future startAt)
    Scheduled --> Queued: timer fires (QueueHost::arm_timer)
    Queued --> Downloading: slot free (QueueManager::promote -> launch)
    Downloading --> Paused: pause_download
    Paused --> Downloading: resume_download
    Downloading --> Muxing: YouTube streams done
    Downloading --> Complete
    Muxing --> Complete
    Downloading --> Error
    Downloading --> Canceled: cancel_download
    Queued --> Canceled: cancel_download (cancel_pending)

    %% Closing the window only hides it (tray); the app keeps downloading.
    %% Tray Quit (shell::quit): pause jobs -> wait ~0.9 s for sidecars -> flush history -> exit.
    state "App quit from the tray, or killed" as Closed
    Downloading --> Closed
    Paused --> Closed
    Muxing --> Closed
    Queued --> Closed
    Scheduled --> Closed

    state "Relaunch: history::restore()" as Restore
    Closed --> Restore
    Restore --> Interrupted: was running, or queued without startAt
    Restore --> Scheduled: startAt in the future (timer re-armed)
    Restore --> Queued: startAt already passed (queue cap applies)
    Restore --> Interrupted: needs header values (not saved to disk)

    Interrupted --> Queued: retry_download (same path -> .idm sidecar -> resume from current)
    Error --> Queued: retry_download
    Canceled --> Queued: retry_download (file was deleted -> fresh start)

    Complete --> [*]: clear_completed / remove_history_entry
    Canceled --> [*]: clear_completed / remove_history_entry
    Error --> [*]: remove_history_entry
    Interrupted --> [*]: remove_history_entry (partial file + sidecar kept)

    note right of Restore
        Sidecar records min(current, written):
        only bytes the flusher already wrote,
        so a kill never leaves holes.
    end note
